WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.293
- Within three seconds
of that happening

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:04.754
my phone was exploding
in my pocket.

00:00:04.754 --> 00:00:06.089
- It was Belichick.
You know that voice.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.757
And he goes, "Steven—"
- "Hi, Steven."

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:08.425
- Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:11.011
- This is the sign of the end

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:14.097
and the birth
of a new blood king.

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:18.893
♪♪♪

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:21.604
I don't wanna do the show.
I don't wanna do it.

00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:23.273
- Let's do it, baby!
- No.

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:25.525
Cuz it—everyone's—
- Saints are alive!

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.403
Let's go, Saints.
- That's where we are.

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:30.196
But that wasn't
the biggest news.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:33.033
The biggest news of the weekend
was about referees.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.492
- Oh!
- We're not talkin' about

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.703
Sarah Thomas
is the first female in the playoffs.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.079
We're talkin' about
this moment—

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.373
3:48 in the fourth quarter.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.417
Patrick Mahomes is gonna
take this snap.

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:43.793
You were focused on Tyreek Hill.

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:45.628
- I was.
I was total fanboy right here.

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:48.048
- And then, all of a sudden,
you're in another stratosphere.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.050
- Man!

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.635
[Laughing]

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:53.928
- Oh my God!
- Look at that

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:55.346
balance in the pocket.

00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:57.265
- Ohhh.
- Stay on the back foot.

00:00:57.265 --> 00:01:00.101
- Dude, this is the first time
you've danced well in your life.

00:01:00.101 --> 00:01:03.313
- How dare you say that, Lefkoe.
- Oh, nature!

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:04.814
Oh my gosh.

00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:06.232
- Thank you, graphics department.
That was great.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.734
- What does it feel like
to be a meme?

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.319
- I, I mean,
I don't even know what to say.

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:11.362
All I can say is,
literally right there

00:01:11.362 --> 00:01:13.114
I was becoming a fanboy.

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:14.657
I was off the white.

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:16.034
But of course it's my fault.

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:18.036
I should've been farther
off the white.

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:21.206
And I've been on sidelines,
like, my whole life

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:22.874
and that's never happened.

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:24.375
- You've never been hit
by a referee—

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:25.794
- Or, like, a coach running down?

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:27.629
- Never. Never. And I was—
I'm not gonna—

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.464
- Did you—cuz it looked
like you were angry.

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:31.591
Did you apologize?
- I was literally apologizing

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.927
as I was skipping backwards.
- "I'm sorry, I'm sorry."

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.428
- Yeah, as I went, "Oh, my bad!

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.514
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!"
I literally did that.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:40.183
And then, you know,
I continued to apologize.

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:42.102
And then it went
into the next play, and I—

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.394
- Did he, did he go,
"Oh, don't worry about it.

00:01:43.394 --> 00:01:44.729
It's totally fine"?
- Totally not.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:47.232
He was pissed off, and—
- How many curses?

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:49.859
- Uh, he—no. So then, yeah.
I think he might've said like

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:51.069
"Get the eff
out of the way," right?

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:52.529
- Yeah.
- And then the next play

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:54.322
I'm continuing to apologize.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:57.200
And I go,
"Man, I'm really sorry.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.868
I'm a dumbass."

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.703
And he looked at me and he goes,
"At least you know it."

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:02.455
- Damn.
- And then he lined over

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.249
and went back to business.
But other refs on the field—

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:05.500
- Did you—
- Knew it was me

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.960
and they were like, chuckling.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.503
- That's such a good burn.
- Damn, that was bad.

00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:10.130
- He set that up so well.
- Damn.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.841
I knew I was in trouble, Lefkoe,
cuz I swear to you

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:15.093
within three seconds
of that happening

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:17.428
my phone was exploding
in my pocket.

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:19.514
And I was like, "Oh, no."
- It was probably my tweets.

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.933
- Everybody saw it, yeah.
- It was amazing.
- Yeah, great, great.

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:24.102
One of my favorite moments
in divisional playoff history.

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:25.478
Really great.
- Yeah, well, you know what else

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.521
is amazing?

00:02:26.521 --> 00:02:29.357
[Laughing]

00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:33.236
Oh, there was a game at 4:40 on
Sunday that was quite enjoyable!

00:02:33.236 --> 00:02:35.155
- I missed it.
I was repotting orchids.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:38.449
- Mr. Drew Brees Hater,
right here!

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:39.742
How many yards did he throw
for in the game?

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:41.494
300. 300.
- I honestly don't know.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.954
- Don't worry,
I'll answer for you.

00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:44.247
OK, here's the first tweet.

00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.748
- Hold on.
So, I wanna say something.

00:02:45.748 --> 00:02:47.792
I have not looked at my mentions
since the game.

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:49.377
I have avoided them completely.

00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:51.462
So I only imagine what people
were saying to me.

00:02:51.462 --> 00:02:53.590
- All right. Well, this is
an intelligent one

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.758
cuz this is Ted, M.D., OK?
- Oh, it's a doctor.

00:02:55.758 --> 00:02:57.385
- Oh, yes. He's a doctor.
And he wrote—

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.726
That's perfect!
Way to go, Ted, M.D.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.769
Did they teach you that—
- Hold on, hold on.

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:08.104
That phrase.
- Yes.

00:03:08.104 --> 00:03:09.439
- "You s--t-talking
Philly rat."

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:10.940
- Right.
- I felt that through the screen

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.859
you know what I mean?
- Yeah, you should. Right.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.694
- That one, damn.
- That was hard-hitting, right.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.237
All right.
- And it's a doctor!

00:03:16.237 --> 00:03:19.032
- Here's another creative name,
50 Shades of Bray.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.909
OK, I like this.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.262
[Laughing]

00:03:41.262 --> 00:03:43.932
- The best part is, is that he
totally went to thesaurus.com

00:03:43.932 --> 00:03:45.225
and looked up "exuberance,"
but then ended it

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.059
and looked up "exuberance,"
but then ended it

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.393
with "Suck it."
- Yes.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.729
- Because really, the first
two sentences—

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.981
- Were good.
- And then it equals "Suck it."

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:53.149
- Yeah, that was pretty good.

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:54.943
Way to go.
- Thanks, Braley.

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:58.404
- And then we got ol' tweet
No. 3 with just the ol'—
- Oh, wow.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.740
- "Oh, hey, up yours."
What the hell's his name again?

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.117
- Mr. Bean.
- Mr. Bean, right.

00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:05.745
Yes, Mr. Bean goin' by, goin',
"Hey, Adam Lefkoe.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.831
My name's Drew Brees
and, uh, eat that."

00:04:08.831 --> 00:04:10.333
- I'm just gonna be honest.
- Yes.

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:12.752
- We are having our
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe" show down

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.004
