like that, they go

00:04:48.079 --> 00:04:50.248
"Eh, OK, we won the Super Bowl
last year.

00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:51.499
We'll see you next year."

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:52.834
- Yeah.
- The rally back, and—

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.127
- I agree.
- Really become, again

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.545
one of the better
teams in football

00:04:55.545 --> 00:04:57.714
and have a chance
to win that game.

00:04:57.714 --> 00:04:59.507
So props to your Eagles.
I'll give you that much.

00:04:59.507 --> 00:05:01.801
- You just witnessed one of
the first genuine moments

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.052
in "Simms &amp; Lefkoe" history.

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:05.388
- All right, let's go.

00:05:05.388 --> 00:05:08.766
Jamal Adams,
and I'm on "Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:11.185
My two guys.

00:05:12.186 --> 00:05:13.146
- All right.
We have Steven Jackson.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.355
We don't wanna waste
any more time.

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:16.107
Just go.
- All right, so here we go.

00:05:16.107 --> 00:05:17.942
You got two teams. You played
two out of the four teams.

00:05:17.942 --> 00:05:19.235
You played the Rams,
the Patriots.

00:05:19.235 --> 00:05:20.987
We'll get to the Patriots
in a second.

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.572
But first of all,
do you root for the Rams?

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:26.117
Like, are you a Rams fan
because of your time there?

00:05:26.117 --> 00:05:27.452
- Yeahhh.
- That's a no.

00:05:27.452 --> 00:05:29.120
- That was a big breath.
- That was a lean back—

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.913
- You saw that body language?
- Yeah, I did.

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:32.248
That was bad body language.

00:05:32.248 --> 00:05:33.958
- It is bad, I know.

00:05:33.958 --> 00:05:35.668
- But you're one of the all-time
greats in Rams history.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:37.837
It's you, Dickerson,
and Gurley and Faulk.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.839
- Well, so wait.
That's where I wanna go.
- Right.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:40.965
- But of course, he's gonna ask
my question now, too

00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:42.383
- But of course, he's gonna ask
my question now, too

00:05:42.383 --> 00:05:44.052
is, do you—
all right.

00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:45.678
So, first of all,
do you root for the Rams?

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.055
Just start there.
- I do.

00:05:47.055 --> 00:05:49.098
But I—
it's bittersweet, right?

00:05:49.098 --> 00:05:50.850
- Yeah?
- It's like, you give them

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.435
almost a decade, nine years

00:05:52.435 --> 00:05:53.936
you give them
everything you have.

00:05:53.936 --> 00:05:55.563
Never better than 8-8.

00:05:55.563 --> 00:05:57.482
- Right.
- Nine seasons

00:05:57.482 --> 00:05:58.566
I had six coaches—
- Right.
- Counting interim coaches.

00:05:58.566 --> 00:06:00.193
I had six coaches—
- Right.
- Counting interim coaches.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:01.778
- Yes.
- So all I know is turnover.

00:06:01.778 --> 00:06:03.321
- Yeah.
- And now to see the success

00:06:03.321 --> 00:06:04.947
of this group.
- Before you is the Greatest

00:06:04.947 --> 00:06:06.532
Show on Turf.
- Yeah.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.451
- After you is Sean McVay
and this offensive explosion.

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:09.786
- Right.
- In-between—

00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:11.871
- Yeah, I'm just the meat.
- Yeah.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.956
Well, I know.
So, so, I do.

00:06:13.956 --> 00:06:16.209
I mean, you're one of the great
running backs of all time.

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.294
You're 18th on the all-time
rushing list.

00:06:18.294 --> 00:06:19.962
- Wild.
- Do you feel like

00:06:19.962 --> 00:06:22.256
you're almost,
like, the forgotten man

00:06:22.256 --> 00:06:24.509
not only as a whole,
but for the Rams?

00:06:24.509 --> 00:06:26.260
Like, I feel like people
just go

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.388
"Marshall Faulk" and "Todd Gurley."

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:30.640
And they forget that you were,
like, a super stud

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.100
in the NFL for a long time.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.519
- Yeah. Well, my
favorite question to fans

00:06:34.519 --> 00:06:36.437
that say they're real fans is,
"Who's the leading rusher

00:06:36.437 --> 00:06:38.064
for the L.A. Rams?"
- Right.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:40.149
- Most people say Eric Dickerson.
It's like, well

00:06:40.149 --> 00:06:42.443
you don't know your history.
You didn't watch me, obviously.

00:06:42.443 --> 00:06:44.112
- Yeah.
- Right.

00:06:44.112 --> 00:06:45.738
- And that's the
frustrating part, is, you know

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.240
I understand
that team leadership

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.699
and team wins come together.

00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:50.118
And I just wasn't a part
of that team.

00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:51.661
- Right.
- But when you talk about

00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:53.996
individual and what a person
put out on the field

00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:55.373
what we worked hard to do?
- Yeah.

00:06:55.373 --> 00:06:56.833
- I just want
some acknowledgement.

00:06:56.833 --> 00:06:58.709
And sometimes I feel like
I get skipped over

00:06:58.709 --> 00:07:00.378
and it's not because
of my talent.

00:07:00.378 --> 00:07:01.838
I know that.
It's just because

00:07:01.838 --> 00:07:03.881
I just had a bad break, man.
- Yeah, yeah that's what happens.

00:07:03.881 --> 00:07:05.425
- Well, we talk about it
all the time.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.885
It's everyone says
that wins isn't a statistic.

00:07:07.885 --> 00:07:09.303
But yet, we treat it like

00:07:09.303 --> 00:07:10.888
it's the greatest statistic
of all time.

00:07:10.888 --> 00:07:13.057
- You're right. Yeah.
- That's kinda how it goes.

00:07:13.057 --> 00:07:15.476
But what's funny is,
is then you go to the Patriots

00:07:15.476 --> 00:07:18.688
which, there's nothing better
than Bill Belichick with a guy

00:07:18.688 --> 00:07:21.315
that hasn't been getting respect
from another team.

00:07:21.315 --> 00:07:23.109
Happened with Corey Dillon.
It happened with

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:25.403
you know, like, every safety,
wide receivers.

00:07:25.403 --> 00:07:27.572
Happened with Chad Johnson,
our friend.

00:07:27.572 --> 00:07:29.657
You go there.

00:07:29.657 --> 00:07:31.951
What was your first meeting
with Belichick?

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.703
Like, what were your—
what was a great

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:36.164
Belichick story
about who he really is?

00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:39.375
- My story of Belichick
is he calls me in December

00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:42.044
LeGarrette Blount goes down,
he gets hurt.

00:07:42.044 --> 00:07:43.713
- That was the injury.
- That was the injury.

00:07:43.713 --> 00:07:46.215
He goes down, and I'm retired
at this point in my head.

00:07:46.215 --> 00:07:47.592
And it's Belichick.
You know that voice.

00:07:47.592 --> 00:07:48.885
It's very distinct.

00:07:48.885 --> 00:07:50.011
And he goes, "Steven—"
- "Hi, Steven."

00:07:50.011 --> 00:07:51.554
- Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:07:51.554 --> 00:07:54.807
He goes, "Steven, uh, I got
a question for you.

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:56.726
Do you wanna play
football again?"

00:07:56.726 --> 00:07:58.060
And I'm like, in my head

00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.896
like, "Of course I do."
- Yeah.

00:07:59.896 --> 00:08:01.689
- But I'm like,
they're in December.

00:08:01.689 --> 00:08:03.274
This is the
New England Patriots

00:08:03.274 --> 00:08:04.484
and I'm a man of pride.

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:05.526
I don't wanna look bad.

00:08:05.526 --> 00:08:07.195
Like, the—my last carry

00:08:07.195 --> 00:08:09.113
I felt I still
looked like myself.

00:08:09.113 --> 00:08:10.406
I didn't wanna get
to New England

00:08:10.406 --> 00:08:11.657
and look like a shell of myself.

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:12.992
- Yeah.
- And then people are like

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.202
"Oh, he's—"
you know, "He's terrible.

00:08:14.202 --> 00:08:15.661
He's trash."
- Yeah, yeah.

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:17.079
- So I was more nervous
about public opinion

00:08:17.079 --> 00:08:18.456
about what I would look like.

00:08:18.456 --> 00:08:20.082
- Mmm.
- So I said, "Coach, you give me

00:08:20.082 --> 00:08:22.376
two weeks to get in shape,
I'll come."

00:08:22.376 --> 00:08:22.835
two weeks to get in shape,
I'll come."

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.170
What was it
like going there

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.755
seeing their day-to-day
preparation

00:08:25.755 --> 00:08:29.217
and specifically, like,
AFC Championship

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:31.302
getting ready for the Broncos
that year

00:08:31.302 --> 00:08:32.595
what that was like being a part

00:08:32.595 --> 00:08:34.222
of that organization
during that time?

00:08:34.222 --> 00:08:35.848
- So, when you get there,
you realize that there's

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:39.393
no place like it in the NFL,
at least my stops.
- Yep.

00:08:39.393 --> 00:08:42.104
There's not a lot of pictures
in the hallways.

00:08:42.104 --> 00:08:45.316
There's not a lot of
"me, me, me," you know?

00:08:45.316 --> 00:08:47.026
But what I found
the most interesting

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:48.736
to your question, is getting
ready for that AFC game

00:08:48.736 --> 00:08:51.572
against the Denver Broncos,
if I recall right

00:08:51.572 --> 00:08:53.157
he asked me to talk to the team.

00:08:53.157 --> 00:08:56.244
And he wanted me to talk to them
about my NFL experience.

00:08:56.244 --> 00:08:58.538
I'm like, "What do I have
to teach these guys," you know?

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:00.998
You guys have been to now eight
consecutive AFC championships.

00:09:00.998 --> 00:09:02.708
- Right.
- Gronkowski's laughing.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:05.419
He goes, "I've never
had not a bye," right?

00:09:05.419 --> 00:09:07.046
- Right.
- I'm like, I've only been

00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:09.048
in the playoffs twice,
first year and last year.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.967
- Yeah.
- And he's laughing like

00:09:10.967 --> 00:09:12.843
"You got a bad break."
- Right.

00:09:12.843 --> 00:09:14.971
- So he asked me to talk
about my plight

00:09:14.971 --> 00:09:16.639
so I'm telling the team
about my story.

00:09:16.639 --> 00:09:20.101
And my story goes,
there's a part of my career

00:09:20.101 --> 00:09:22.728
where I won six games
in three years.

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:23.521
- Wow.

00:09:23.521 --> 00:09:26.065
I'm talking to the team
about me winning six games

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:27.275
in three years.
- Yeah.

00:09:27.275 --> 00:09:28.568
- And you could just hear
a pin drop.

00:09:28.568 --> 00:09:29.694
And they just couldn't believe
the amount

00:09:29.694 --> 00:09:30.528
And they just couldn't believe
the amount

00:09:30.528 --> 00:09:32.113
of eight consecutive
1,000 yards rushing

00:09:32.113 --> 00:09:32.613
of eight consecutive
1,000 yards rushing

00:09:32.613 --> 00:09:34.824
but the lack of wins
to go with it.

00:09:34.824 --> 00:09:35.700
but the lack of wins
to go with it.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.245
It's almost like those guys
wanted to win that game for me.

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:40.705
- Yeah.
- And that was a special moment

00:09:40.705 --> 00:09:40.871
- Yeah.
- And that was a special moment

00:09:40.871 --> 00:09:43.165
because I didn't think
my story was anything.

00:09:43.165 --> 00:09:44.917
I thought I was just privileged
to be there.

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:47.211
But to see that it was twofold,
and that they wanted me

00:09:47.211 --> 00:09:50.131
to kinda cap off
my career with a win.

00:09:50.131 --> 00:09:51.632
- Sure.
- It meant a lot to me

00:09:51.632 --> 00:09:53.467
and, you know,
I'll always forever be grateful.

00:09:53.467 --> 00:09:56.679
- And you got a touchdown in the
AFC Championship Game in Denver.
- Yeah.

00:09:56.679 --> 00:09:58.931
- Do you think he was
trying to, like

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:01.767
you know, Belichick,
like, is he trying to show, like

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.394
"Hey, you guys are spoiled."
- Absolutely he was.

00:10:03.394 --> 00:10:05.229
- "And look how grateful
this—." Yeah, OK.

00:10:05.229 --> 00:10:06.606
- You can't take it
for granted, right?

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:07.189
- Right, right.
- And I think, if you're

00:10:07.189 --> 00:10:07.565
- Right, right.
- And I think, if you're

00:10:07.565 --> 00:10:09.358
Gronkowski, for example,
he doesn't know anything else.

00:10:09.358 --> 00:10:10.401
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:10:10.401 --> 00:10:11.736
- He only knows Brady, Belichick

00:10:11.736 --> 00:10:13.446
and playoff wins,
you know what I'm saying?

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:15.865
- He assumes that Cincinnati's
like that.

00:10:15.865 --> 00:10:17.199
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:10:17.199 --> 00:10:18.492
- Now they're in
a similar situation.

00:10:18.492 --> 00:10:20.328
They haven't been
in that situation

00:10:20.328 --> 00:10:23.873
since your speech and that game
of a road AFC Championship Game.

00:10:23.873 --> 00:10:27.835
And since 2004, they've been to
the playoffs, like, 13 times.

00:10:27.835 --> 00:10:31.422
This has only happened three
times, and the Patriots are 0-3.

00:10:31.422 --> 00:10:33.257
- 0-3 on the road.
- I'm curious

00:10:33.257 --> 00:10:37.094
what is Belichick like the week
of an AFC Championship Game?

00:10:37.094 --> 00:10:39.096
- Very relaxed. Everyone—
- Really?

00:10:39.096 --> 00:10:41.265
- And I would say the whole team.

00:10:41.265 --> 00:10:43.142
That's the, that was the other
thing that was impressive.

00:10:43.142 --> 00:10:45.853
From the running back coach
to the special teams coach

00:10:45.853 --> 00:10:47.605
to even just
the team chaplain, it is—

00:10:47.605 --> 00:10:50.191
- Nothing's different.
- Nothing's different there.

00:10:50.191 --> 00:10:51.734
It is normal.

00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:54.195
Football in January and February
is normal to them.

00:10:54.195 --> 00:10:55.696
- It's the regular season.
- Sounds like you were

00:10:55.696 --> 00:10:57.490
in a bizarro world—
- I was.

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.325
- Where you're like,
"I've never been here before.

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:01.327
This is insane." And everyone's
like, "It's Tuesday, Steven.

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:02.828
Take a seat."
- Yeah, I'm normally

00:11:02.828 --> 00:11:03.996
looking at my passport.

00:11:03.996 --> 00:11:05.289
I'm in Costa Rica
somewhere, right?

00:11:05.289 --> 00:11:06.582
- Yeah.
- And they're like, "Nah, man.

00:11:06.582 --> 00:11:08.626
This is divisional round week."

00:11:08.626 --> 00:11:11.379
- My only other thing is

00:11:11.379 --> 00:11:16.717
if you could say anything to
the basketball Stephen Jackson

00:11:16.717 --> 00:11:18.928
what would you say to him?
- Stak5, what's up?

00:11:18.928 --> 00:11:19.470
what would you say to him?
- Stak5, what's up?

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:20.930
- Do you guys, like, talk?

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:22.348
Do the Steven Jacksons
talk to each other?

00:11:22.348 --> 00:11:23.849
- No, we haven't talked in a while.

00:11:23.849 --> 00:11:25.893
We've, we ran into
each other before.

00:11:25.893 --> 00:11:28.562
Um, oddly enough,
it was in a nightclub

00:11:28.562 --> 00:11:31.774
in San Antonio and I—
we got each other's bills.

00:11:31.774 --> 00:11:33.401
- Really? That's how you—
Did you even—

00:11:33.401 --> 00:11:35.986
- You don't wanna mess with
that NBA money, man.

00:11:35.986 --> 00:11:37.405
- Yeah, yeah.
I'm like, no, no, no.

00:11:37.405 --> 00:11:38.781
I'm not guaranteed.
I'll take the small one.

00:11:38.781 --> 00:11:40.116
- I didn't order three
Ace of Spades.

00:11:40.116 --> 00:11:41.784
- Right.
So there's been some mixups.

00:11:41.784 --> 00:11:43.494
- That's unbelievable.
I love it.

00:11:43.494 --> 00:11:44.286
We're happy to have you, man.

00:11:44.286 --> 00:11:45.705
- Thank you, man.
- Yeah, thanks for coming by.

00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:46.664
- For real.
- Seriously.

00:11:47.748 --> 00:11:49.041
- Hi, I'm LaMarr Woodley.

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.710
And you're watching
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.379
Let's go.
Lefkoe?

00:11:53.379 --> 00:11:54.672
Let's go, all the same.

00:11:54.672 --> 00:11:55.631
Just let's go.

00:11:56.465 --> 00:11:58.467
- What do ya know?
Lefkoe's Locks have been

00:11:58.467 --> 00:12:00.052
hittin' in the playoffs.

00:12:00.052 --> 00:12:02.888
I haven't needed anybody,
let alone somebody.

00:12:02.888 --> 00:12:07.977
7-1, and for the season,
I'm 34-34-3.

00:12:07.977 --> 00:12:09.437
Oooh, .500 feels good.

00:12:09.437 --> 00:12:10.771
No thanks to Allie.

00:12:10.771 --> 00:12:12.356
He's 0-2 in the playoffs

00:12:12.356 --> 00:12:14.233
and you know I'm lettin' him
hear about it.

00:12:16.861 --> 00:12:19.363
This man is 0-2 in the playoffs.

00:12:19.363 --> 00:12:23.325
He's gone from Allie the Oracle
to Allie the Mush.

00:12:23.325 --> 00:12:26.495
And I'm 7-1 against the spread
in the playoffs, Allie.

00:12:26.495 --> 00:12:28.164
I'm open for advice
if you need it.

00:12:28.164 --> 00:12:32.376
- Your team is out of it, though.
- Why—?
- So 7-1 means nothing.

00:12:32.376 --> 00:12:34.670
- It means a lot to my ego.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:37.882
Chiefs are favored by three at home
against the Patriots.

00:12:37.882 --> 00:12:40.426
- Chiefs-Patriots,
I don't have a pick.

00:12:40.426 --> 00:12:42.261
I need some,
I need some help with this one.

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:44.263
- Timeout.
- I need a little bit of help.

00:12:44.263 --> 00:12:46.056
- Are you asking for
a little Lefkoe guidance?

00:12:46.056 --> 00:12:47.516
- Little bit.

00:12:47.516 --> 00:12:48.851
- Cuz it would be my pleasure.
- Little bit.

00:12:48.851 --> 00:12:50.853
I'm leaning Chiefs.
- OK.

00:12:50.853 --> 00:12:52.354
- But it's tough for me
to go against Tom Brady.

00:12:52.354 --> 00:12:53.814
What do you think?

00:12:53.814 --> 00:12:55.316
- My thing is, is that Tom
doesn't have to play

00:12:55.316 --> 00:12:57.443
in the championship games
on the road often.

00:12:57.443 --> 00:13:00.362
He's only had three road games
since 2004.

00:13:00.362 --> 00:13:03.032
Broncos, Steelers, Colts,
I believe.

00:13:03.032 --> 00:13:05.534
And he's lost all three of them.

00:13:05.534 --> 00:13:08.162
I would go Chiefs
because I think

00:13:08.162 --> 00:13:10.372
it's Patrick Mahomes at home.

00:13:10.372 --> 00:13:12.041
I don't know.
I love that kid.

00:13:12.041 --> 00:13:13.667
I feel the magic.

00:13:13.667 --> 00:13:16.754
- Patrick Mahomes at home.
Arrowhead, Arrowhead.

00:13:16.754 --> 00:13:18.339
The first game
was in Foxborough.

00:13:18.339 --> 00:13:20.633
- Yes.
- Chiefs.

00:13:20.633 --> 00:13:22.301
- Did you see that?
Did you see his eyes?

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:23.594
- Gotta go Chiefs. Gotta go Chiefs.
- He White Walker-ed.

00:13:23.594 --> 00:13:25.638
He went, "Chiefs."
- Chiefs.

00:13:25.638 --> 00:13:28.474
I'm gonna let you know now
though, if Tom Brady wins—

00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:30.059
- New England
with the Super Bowl.

00:13:30.059 --> 00:13:31.519
You don't even have to come.

00:13:31.519 --> 00:13:32.853
Lettin' you know now.
- Wow.

00:13:32.853 --> 00:13:35.272
I felt Oracle emanation
right there.

00:13:35.272 --> 00:13:37.149
That was really serious.
- Sounds crazy.

00:13:37.149 --> 00:13:38.943
I'm goin' against them
this week, but if they win

00:13:38.943 --> 00:13:40.361
I'm goin' with them
to the Super Bowl.

00:13:40.361 --> 00:13:42.363
- Typical Allie hedging.
What a mush.

00:13:42.363 --> 00:13:44.740
What a mush, this guy.
- It's all right.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:45.950
Don't worry.
We'll be fine.

00:13:47.117 --> 00:13:49.537
- So Allie finally comes
to his senses

00:13:49.537 --> 00:13:51.163
listens to what I have to say

00:13:51.163 --> 00:13:52.706
and he's takin'
the Chiefs minus-3.

00:13:52.706 --> 00:13:53.707
- OK.
- Gonna be honest

00:13:53.707 --> 00:13:55.376
Three is a lot of points.

00:13:55.376 --> 00:13:57.002
I'm gonna wait until Patriots
bettors knock it down

00:13:57.002 --> 00:13:58.170
and then I'm gonna bet
on the Chiefs.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.505
- Yeah, I hear that.

00:13:59.505 --> 00:14:00.798
- But you think the Chiefs
are gonna win.

00:14:00.798 --> 00:14:02.466
- I do think
the Chiefs are gonna win.

00:14:02.466 --> 00:14:03.968
I mean, both of these games
should be really close.

00:14:03.968 --> 00:14:05.511
- It's so dumb, betting
against the Patriots.

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:07.555
- I know. But I do.
If you made me bet on this game

00:14:07.555 --> 00:14:08.889
I would take the Chiefs.

00:14:08.889 --> 00:14:11.100
Maybe to win
a four-point game, 34-30.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.935
- OK.
- 35-31, something like that.

00:14:12.935 --> 00:14:14.812
- So you see high scoring.
- Yeah, somewhere along there.

00:14:14.812 --> 00:14:17.731
- Both games are rematches
of amazing regular-season games.

00:14:17.731 --> 00:14:21.443
In those two games,
over 160 points scored.

00:14:21.443 --> 00:14:23.237
But I don't think it's gonna be
the same game

00:14:23.237 --> 00:14:24.822
and I know
that you definitely don't.

00:14:24.822 --> 00:14:26.198
- No.
- So, Saints-Rams.

00:14:26.198 --> 00:14:27.783
- Yes.
- What's gonna be different about

00:14:27.783 --> 00:14:29.285
that game from the first match?

00:14:29.285 --> 00:14:30.786
- Well, I think the first thing
that jumps out

00:14:30.786 --> 00:14:33.080
to me is one stat line
with Michael Thomas

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.624
12 receptions, 211 yards, right?

00:14:35.624 --> 00:14:37.459
Had the unbelievable
performance

00:14:37.459 --> 00:14:39.879
burned Marcus Peters in one of
the biggest plays of the game.

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:41.589
Sean Payton said
they liked the matchup.

00:14:41.589 --> 00:14:43.257
We're gonna see
that little rivalry flamed up.

00:14:43.257 --> 00:14:45.926
- Talib didn't play in that game.
- Talib did not play.

00:14:45.926 --> 00:14:48.888
And the other big point,
Lefkoe, is this.

00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:52.308
The Rams don't play those style
of defenses anymore.

00:14:52.308 --> 00:14:55.102
They are not really a matchup,
man-to-man defense

00:14:55.102 --> 00:14:57.396
like they were back in Week 11.

00:14:57.396 --> 00:15:00.190
Now they have really become
more of a zone team.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.860
We're gonna play sound coverages
in the back end

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:04.904
let our front four
get after the quarterback.

00:15:04.904 --> 00:15:06.405
- Sure.
- So, hey, Michael Thomas

00:15:06.405 --> 00:15:08.032
he's extremely hard to defend.

00:15:08.032 --> 00:15:10.242
We know that not only
because he's a good player

00:15:10.242 --> 00:15:12.369
but Sean Payton
moves him around everywhere.

00:15:12.369 --> 00:15:14.288
- You know what else, though?
- So I think he could be around

00:15:14.288 --> 00:15:17.207
100 yards,
but no way around 200 yards.

00:15:17.207 --> 00:15:19.585
- That was also the
Sheldon Rankins breakout game.

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:21.253
- It was.
- He won't play in this game.

00:15:21.253 --> 00:15:23.047
- He's not there, right.
- So that's big, too.

00:15:23.047 --> 00:15:24.548
- Crazy stat about that game?
No sacks, right?

00:15:24.548 --> 00:15:26.050
Can you believe that,
in that type of game?

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.468
- That's not happening again.
- That's insane.

00:15:27.468 --> 00:15:28.761
No, I would not say
that happens again.

00:15:28.761 --> 00:15:29.929
- What happened
in Chiefs-Patriots

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:31.221
during the regular season

00:15:31.221 --> 00:15:32.806
that's definitely
not happening on Sunday?

00:15:32.806 --> 00:15:34.433
- I think the big thing
to look at there is

00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:38.145
there was 13 total rush attempts
by the Kansas City Chiefs

00:15:38.145 --> 00:15:39.730
running backs
in that football game.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.398
- That's Andy Reid, man.
- Yes, that's Andy Reid.

00:15:41.398 --> 00:15:42.775
We know that.

00:15:42.775 --> 00:15:44.902
So why I say
that won't happen again

00:15:44.902 --> 00:15:46.654
the first reason is this.

00:15:46.654 --> 00:15:48.405
The Chiefs have been trying
to be a more balanced team.

00:15:48.405 --> 00:15:50.157
We saw that last week
against the Colts.

00:15:50.157 --> 00:15:53.577
Damien Williams had some success
running between the tackles.

00:15:53.577 --> 00:15:55.496
So I think they've been
underneath the center

00:15:55.496 --> 00:15:56.789
with Patrick Mahomes.

00:15:56.789 --> 00:15:58.499
- Yeah.
- The attempts are very important

00:15:58.499 --> 00:16:00.542
because when you become
one-dimensional against

00:16:00.542 --> 00:16:03.295
Bill Belichick and company,
you're in deep trouble.

00:16:03.295 --> 00:16:04.755
If they can just go,
"Oh, you're gonna throw

00:16:04.755 --> 00:16:06.507
the ball every down"

00:16:06.507 --> 00:16:08.092
they're gonna come up with
a million different coverages

00:16:08.092 --> 00:16:10.177
to confuse Mahomes,
doubles, blitzes

00:16:10.177 --> 00:16:12.888
everything under the moon, OK?

00:16:12.888 --> 00:16:15.891
So the big thing there
would be the attempts

00:16:15.891 --> 00:16:18.602
because it keeps
the Patriots defense honest.

00:16:18.602 --> 00:16:20.437
And then with Mahomes
under center

00:16:20.437 --> 00:16:22.606
one of the great things
about being under center

00:16:22.606 --> 00:16:25.317
and running the ball
is the play-action passes.

00:16:25.317 --> 00:16:27.903
And we've seen that a little
more from them as of late, too

00:16:27.903 --> 00:16:30.990
to get Tyreek down the field,
Kelce down the field.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.617
But can Andy Reid do it?
Will he stay with it?

00:16:33.617 --> 00:16:35.285
Because you know
as an Eagles fan

00:16:35.285 --> 00:16:37.037
he loves to throw the ball.

00:16:37.037 --> 00:16:38.747
But when they played in the
Super Bowl, Patriots-Eagles,

00:16:38.747 --> 00:16:40.708
he threw the ball
50-plus-something times.

00:16:40.708 --> 00:16:41.917
- Yes.
- He does that again

00:16:41.917 --> 00:16:43.669
they're in trouble.

00:16:43.669 --> 00:16:45.337
Or if they rush the ball
for 13 attempts or less

00:16:45.337 --> 00:16:47.381
that means they got down early
and had to throw

00:16:47.381 --> 00:16:49.049
and they're in trouble anyways.

00:16:49.049 --> 00:16:50.384
That would be my two cents.

00:16:50.384 --> 00:16:52.177
- Your analysis is fine.
- Oh, thanks.

00:16:52.177 --> 00:16:55.723
- But something is happening
Sunday night that scares me

00:16:55.723 --> 00:16:57.057
and I don't know
what it means yet.

00:16:57.057 --> 00:16:59.018
- Yeah.
- Apparently, it's gonna happen

00:16:59.018 --> 00:17:01.895
during the Chiefs-Patriots game
over Arrowhead.

00:17:01.895 --> 00:17:04.815
- Yep.
- A super blood wolf moon—

00:17:04.815 --> 00:17:07.234
- And with the arctic blast.
- Is happening

00:17:07.234 --> 00:17:08.569
during the game.

00:17:08.569 --> 00:17:12.031
- Yes.
- I don't know if this is going

00:17:12.031 --> 00:17:14.867
to be Belichick
using the universe

00:17:14.867 --> 00:17:17.661
to suck the powers
out of Patrick Mahomes

00:17:17.661 --> 00:17:20.914
